WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.330
All right, it's time for Drew's News.

2
00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:06.300
Your daily news stir fry with that good news sizzle.

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.540
And here with me is my trusty co-pilot,

4
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:09.798
Rossy Ross Mathews.

5
00:00:09.798 --> 00:00:11.513
Hi, everybody!

6
00:00:11.513 --> 00:00:12.346
Hey, Drew.

7
00:00:12.346 --> 00:00:14.674
(audience clapping)

8
00:00:14.674 --> 00:00:15.507
I know.

9
00:00:15.507 --> 00:00:17.750
I love you.
I love you.

10
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.500
We're starting with the Beautiful Issue

11
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:20.540
of "People" magazine.

12
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.850
Everybody gets so excited with that.

13
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:24.757
And guess what?
Oh look, yes.

14
00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:29.040
It's none other than Dame Helen Mirren.

15
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.380
There's also a really special story inside

16
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.180
that continues to celebrate women.

17
00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.760
It gives a little inside look

18
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.480
into the favorite besties for all of us, Oprah and Gayle.

19
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.590
They're finally telling their origin story

20
00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:45.410
of the beautiful friendship

21
00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:49.390
that we've all come to know as, "That's my Gayle."

22
00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:52.810
It all started 46 years ago on a snowy night in Baltimore.

23
00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:55.000
Oprah was 21, Gayle was 22.

24
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.160
And the two young newsies

25
00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:00.473 line:15%
were following their dreams at WJTZ-TV.

26
00:01:02.065 --> 00:01:06.340 line:15%
And then, this blizzard hit and Oprah invited Gayle over

27
00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:09.510 line:15%
and they were like up all night chatting.

28
00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:12.200 line:15%
They had this great kind of evening

29
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.960 line:15%
that the weather brought them together

30
00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.480 line:15%
and the rest is history.

31
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:16.400 line:15%
You just never know

32
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.400 line:15%
when you're gonna meet your next bestie.

33
00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.760 line:15%
You know, I've met besties poolside.

34
00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:21.610
I've met 'em at a bar.

35
00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:24.190
I've met 'em at this very desk right here.

36
00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:25.509
Aw!
You never know

37
00:01:25.509 --> 00:01:26.921
when you're gonna meet a bestie.

38
00:01:26.921 --> 00:01:27.754
Think about that.

39
00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:28.840
Who could you meet next

40
00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:30.520
and they could be your next best friend?

41
00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:31.560
I love that idea.

42
00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:34.330
All right, next, we've got women bringing major changes

43
00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:37.443
to the MLB in today's Sports! Sports! Sports!

44
00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.253
Been too long

45
00:01:39.253 --> 00:01:40.709
since we've done sports.
Gives me withdrawals.

46
00:01:40.709 --> 00:01:42.937
I know.
We need it back.

47
00:01:42.937 --> 00:01:44.690
Well, "The Wall Street Journal" reports

48
00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:47.350
this season there's a new record in baseball.

49
00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:50.850
Listen to this, 11 of the on-field coaches

50
00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:53.890 line:15%
across the Majors and Minors are women.

51
00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:54.825 line:15%
Yep.

52
00:01:54.825 --> 00:01:57.790 line:15%
(audience cheering)
It's pretty amazing.

53
00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.350 line:15%
Yeah, Drew, yeah, yeah, yeah.

54
00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:02.860 line:15%
Put this into perspective a little bit,

55
00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.760 line:15%
since 2018, as recently as that,

56
00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.340
there have been zero, there were zero female coaches

57
00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:10.230
and now there's 11.
That's so crazy.

58
00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:13.480
That's just four years ago.
Yes.

59
00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:16.120
So think about where we could be four years from now.

60
00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:16.959
That's what I like to think about.

61
00:02:16.959 --> 00:02:19.433
Double it, 22.
Hello, triple it.

62
00:02:19.433 --> 00:02:22.433
(audience clapping)

63
00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:25.380
Let's shout out some of these coaches.

64
00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.020
This season, Alyssa Nakken became the very first woman ever

65
00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:29.740
to coach an MLB game for the Giants.

66
00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:32.120
By the way, she looks so cool.

67
00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:34.130
Right, and the Yankees just promoted

68
00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.155
Rachel Balkovec to manager

69
00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:38.670
of the Tampa Tarpons.
Yes!

70
00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:42.120
She's the first woman to lead a team in the Minors.

71
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:44.410
And, MLB, we say keep it up.

72
00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:45.560
That's how you play ball.

73
00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.171
Yes, please.
Yes, that's exactly right.

74
00:02:48.171 --> 00:02:49.870
Mhmm.
(audience clapping)

75
00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:52.453 line:15%
(upbeat music)

